text:
Maya: Quick unblock request — PR https://github.com/redwood-inference/redwood/pull/2890 is failing gofmt on a small API shim. It's basically a one-line change but formatter wants to reflow comments. Can someone with merge rights approve or advise? I can either adjust code or add a formatter exception.

Devon: @Maya can you paste the failing diff? :eyes: 

Maya: Here are the offending bits:

```go
// User-facing shim to adapt new response shape.
// TODO: remove after next release
func adaptResponse(r *response) *apiResponse {
    return &apiResponse{ID: r.ID, Text: r.Text}
}
```

gofmt suggests wrapping long comment lines and adding a blank line before the func.

Sam: If it's just the comment wrapping, prefer changing the comment to one-line. Formatter exceptions are a footgun. e.g.

```go
// Adapter for legacy response shape.
func adaptResponse(r *response) *apiResponse {
    return &apiResponse{ID: r.ID, Text: r.Text}
}
```

Priya: Agree with Sam. Also tests are green? @ci-bot?

ci-bot: build/test — all checks passed :white_check_mark:

Devon: If Maya can push the one-line comment patch I'll approve. Otherwise I can do it quickly.

Maya: Pushed fix and ran `gofmt -w` locally. PR updated: https://github.com/redwood-inference/redwood/pull/2890

Lucy: LGTM :shipit: will merge during next merge window. @Devon you ok with immediate merge?

Devon: Yep, go ahead. :+1: 

Maya: Thanks all! I'll follow up to remove the TODO in a follow-up PR.
